warning: predefined identifier is only valid inside function: `__func__` [-Wpredefined-identifier-outside-function]
 --> sema-predefined-outside-function.c:1:20
  |
1 | const char *name = __func__;
  |                    ^^^^^^^^ used outside a function
  |
  = note: C99 §6.4.2.2p1: __func__ names the enclosing function; GCC and Clang extend this to __FUNCTION__ and __PRETTY_FUNCTION__ and use an empty or `top level` string outside one

